<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul issues licenses for 35 futures brokers.</title>
<headline>Seoul issues licenses for 35 futures brokers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea has issued provisional futures broking licences to 35 local companies, the Ministry of Finance and Economy said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The licence will allow holders to enter the futures brokerage business both overseas and domestically, when a local futures exchange is set up.</p>
<p>The exchange is expected to open in the second half of 1998, the statement said.</p>
</text>
